## Lab 2 — Check a Specific Rule

```powershell
Get-NetFirewallRule | Select-Object DisplayName, Enabled, Direction, Action
```

Observe:

```text
Display Name
Enabled
Direction
Action
```

---

## Lab 3 — Network Connection + Firewall Thinking

Use:

```cmd
netstat -ano
```

Find an established connection and identify:

```text
Source IP
Source Port
Destination IP
Destination Port
Protocol
State
PID
```

Then think about which firewall rule would need to allow or deny that traffic.

